2026-10-01T00:00:06Z (RFD66606-2294) 'agent knowledge lives in RFDs, not in desk memory
 # tags: rfd:details-title, rfd:no-final-newline
 Text:RFD2294  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-01T00:00:07Z (RFD66606-2294) 'What any agent needs to know about V-Sekai-fire and chibifire-stages, their repositories, the headset and the services lives in an RFD in this repository: the RFD that owns the topic, or this one when none does. A desk's local memory keeps only what is true of that desk alone, such as its paths, its identities and its tools. A local note about a generic rule names the RFD that states it.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2294  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-01T00:00:08Z (RFD66606-2294) '- RFD66606-2200, the desk agent's ReBAC rows.
 # tags: rfd:related
 Text:RFD2294  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-01T00:00:09Z (RFD66606-2294) '- RFD66606-2363 to RFD66606-2381 and RFD66606-2413 to RFD66606-2419, the rules this RFD held before the split, one RFD each.
 # tags: rfd:related
 Text:RFD2294  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-01T00:00:10Z (RFD66606-2294) 'Writing a generic rule down
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2294  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-01T00:00:11Z (RFD66606-2294) 'An agent that learns a generic rule writes it into the RFD in the same session, through a pull request like any other change.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2294  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-01T00:00:12Z (RFD66606-2294) 'What lived on one desk
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2294  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-01T00:00:13Z (RFD66606-2294) 'On 2026-10-01 the operator's rules for locomotion, offline deployment, video and the station lived only on the Mac desk, and those for where compute runs and for binary translation only on the Windows desks, so no session saw all of them.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2294  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-01T00:00:14Z (RFD66606-2294) 'Starting out in the workspace
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2294  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-01T00:00:15Z (RFD66606-2294) 'A new agent, a small local model included, starts here and does one step at a time. It begins right after the bootstrap script has run.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2294  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-01T00:00:16Z (RFD66606-2294) '0. The bootstrap leaves a workspace root holding `.repo/`, `AGENTS.md` and the placed projects. Every path below is relative to that root. `ls .repo` and `repo list` confirm it. If `repo`, `elixir`, `mix` or `python` is missing, ask the operator; don't install tools yourself.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2294  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-01T00:00:17Z (RFD66606-2294) '1. Read `AGENTS.md` at the workspace root, then this RFD.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2294  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-01T00:00:18Z (RFD66606-2294) '2. The workspace is a `repo` client. `.repo/manifests/default.xml` (the taskweft manifest repository) places every project on a side of the hexagon: `2-contract/`, `3-interactor/`, `4-entities/`, `5-repository/`, `6-datasource/`, `7-service/`. `repo list` shows what is placed.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2294  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-01T00:00:19Z (RFD66606-2294) '3. Sync with `elixir .repo/manifests/sync.exs . --preflight` first, then `elixir .repo/manifests/sync.exs .`. A project the preflight names as blocking gets a decision from the operator, not a guess. One that blocks because another session works in it moves its branch to a worktree, uncommitted edits carried by `git stash`, and then syncs (operator, 2026-10-18).
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2294  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-01T00:00:20Z (RFD66606-2294) '4. Never edit a placed checkout in place. Make a worktree in a scratch directory on a new `dev/<topic>` branch: `git -C <project> worktree add <scratch>/<name> -b dev/<topic> <remote>/main`, using the project's own remote and default branch.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2294  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-01T00:00:21Z (RFD66606-2294) '5. Commit subjects are sentence-case prose with no `feat:` prefix and no trailing period, forks included (RFD66606-2026). Commits and pull requests carry no Claude attribution: no `Co-Authored-By: Claude` trailer and no "Generated with Claude Code" line. Credit to people stays, such as a co-author trailer for the person whose work a commit carries. "Interchangeable sessions" below names the commit author and how to strip a footer a tool appends. Push only the feature branch, and open the pull request in V-Sekai-fire or chibifire-stages, where the operator merges it.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2294  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-01T00:00:22Z (RFD66606-2294) '6. Remove the worktree when the pull request is open.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2294  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-01T00:00:23Z (RFD66606-2294) 'An RFD is amended in `rfd/NNNN-slug.exs` of &{repo("manuals-weftspun")}, never in the rendered Markdown, which is a build artifact:
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2294  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-01T00:00:24Z (RFD66606-2294) '1. Find the RFD that owns the topic with `grep -l <word> rfd/*.exs`. Use this one when none does.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2294  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-01T00:00:25Z (RFD66606-2294) '2. Edit its `decision` or one of its `details` blocks in the tenseless present (RFD66606-2172). A statement that is no longer true is deleted, not retracted. Name the operator and date for an operator's decision.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2294  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-01T00:00:26Z (RFD66606-2294) '3. A new RFD takes the next serial in `SERIALS.exs` and carries the sentence "This RFD was drafted by an AI and read by a human before it shipped."
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2294  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-01T00:00:27Z (RFD66606-2294) '4. Run `mix rfd.render`, `python scripts/check_tropes.py --base <remote>/main` and `python scripts/check-rfd-structure.py`. All three pass before the push.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2294  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-01T00:00:28Z (RFD66606-2294) '5. Keep product names and other organisations' issue or PR references out of the text, and cite an upstream change by its bare commit SHA.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2294  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-01T00:00:29Z (RFD66606-2294) 'A worked example, typed into Git Bash on the Windows desk. It adds a sentence to this RFD:
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2294  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-01T00:00:30Z (RFD66606-2294) '    cd <workspace root>/2-contract/manuals-weftspun
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2294  1 LINE
 Text:Written

