2026-10-01T00:00:45Z (RFD66606-2294) 'The push names the hooks directory by absolute path because a placed checkout's `.git` is a link into `.repo/projects/`, which Git Bash cannot follow. Given the relative path, the pre-push hook dies before running its gates. Never skip the hook with `--no-verify`. With no GitHub credentials, stop after the commit and give the operator the branch name. When any step fails, stop and ask the operator rather than guess.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2294  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-01T00:00:46Z (RFD66606-2294) 'The work queue
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2294  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-01T00:00:47Z (RFD66606-2294) 'The agent sessions share one work-stealing queue, the issues labelled `worksteal` on &{repo("contract-zone-backend")}. Its protocol is pinned there as #58. An agent works its own queue newest first, and with nothing unclaimed steals the oldest unclaimed, unpinned issue from the fullest queue. A pinned issue needs one desk's hardware or credentials and is never stolen. The queue applies backpressure: a queue holding three or more open issues, pinned ones included, is full, its agent files nothing new and finishes first, a follow-up found mid-task becomes a checklist line in the issue that found it, and an operator request is still filed, with the queue's depth reported back so the operator can say what waits.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2294  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-01T00:00:48Z (RFD66606-2294) 'Interchangeable sessions
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2294  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-01T00:00:49Z (RFD66606-2294) 'Any agent session, on a desk or in the cloud, can pick up any task another session started, because each follows the practices below and reads them here rather than from its own memory. A practice another RFD owns is named here and stated there. A desk's memory, a project's instructions, a skill or `CLAUDE.md` points at this section instead of restating it.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2294  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-01T00:00:50Z (RFD66606-2294) '- Attribution. Commits, pull requests, issue comments and reviews carry no agent credit: no agent `Co-Authored-By` trailer, no session link and no "Generated with" or "Generated by" footer. Commits are authored as `K. S. Ernest (iFire) Lee <32321+fire@users.noreply.github.com>`. The GitHub connector and `gh` append a footer on create, so each body is rewritten with an update call and read back before the task moves on, and `dot-claude`'s `hooks/strip_claude_footer.py` prompts that rewrite after every create (operator, 2026-10-02).
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2294  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-01T00:00:51Z (RFD66606-2294) '- Where a session posts. Pull requests, issues, comments, reviews and discussions go only to repositories in V-Sekai-fire and chibifire-stages. A fix to a fork lands in our fork, and nothing is sent upstream. Reading another organisation's code is fine (operator, 2026-10-05).
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2294  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-01T00:00:52Z (RFD66606-2294) '- Automation. A new driver, gate or sheet builder is a plain Elixir script (`.exs`). Python appears only as a thin worker where a library has no other binding, such as Mitsuba's renderer. A cloud session runs the Elixir gates on CI's pinned toolchain, OTP 29 and Elixir 1.20.4 through `erlef/setup-beam`, never on a distribution's packaged Elixir (operator, 2026-10-02).
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2294  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-01T00:00:53Z (RFD66606-2294) '- Where work runs. A cloud session has no GPU and takes CPU-only work: headless Godot gates, the godot-sandbox tests, CPU Mitsuba (`llvm_ad_rgb`), the cloth fit on its CPU backend, and blend-shape matching through &{repo("contract-lbfgsb")}. Its testing blocklists software GPU emulators: lavapipe and llvmpipe, SwiftShader, WARP, and Vulkan or Metal emulation. Work that needs a GPU (the persona, XR and headset runs, compute-rd and ggml runs, GPU sheet renders, macOS binaries) goes to the GPU desk rather than to an emulator. Timings are reported with milliseconds per frame (operator, 2026-10-02).
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2294  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-01T00:00:54Z (RFD66606-2294) '- GPU Cloud and GPU-Free Cloud. Work split between the GPU desk's session ("GPU Cloud") and a cloud session ("GPU-Free Cloud") is one checklist in one issue, as on `contract-zone-backend#114`. Each session ticks only its own items and comments when it starts, finishes or is blocked on one, with times in RFD66606-2295's form. Neither takes the other's items.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2294  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-01T00:00:55Z (RFD66606-2294) '- Branches. Every branch a session works on starts with a stage: `dev/`, `beta/`, `rc/` or `release/`, and `archived/` once its work is parked or superseded, whatever name the session was handed (operator, 2026-10-12). No `feat/`, `fix/`, `wip/`, `main/` or bare names.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2294  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-01T00:00:56Z (RFD66606-2294) '- Capability-scoped workers. A worker session holds the capabilities its task needs as RFD66606-2200 tuples, and default deny covers the rest. A peer's request never widens a worker's rows.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2294  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-01T00:00:57Z (RFD66606-2294) '- Contact sheets. Release contact sheets are videos: the `sphere_hammersley_sequence` views are the columns and the fitting sequence is the frames. A CI job that shows a sheet renders it in that job and uploads it with `actions/upload-artifact`, so the sheet belongs to the run and the commit that made it. The colour reference is the lookdev-24 chart, &{repo("entities-sakuragaoka-station")}'s `tools/calib/chart24.json`, and no commercial chart's trademark appears in code or documents. RFD66606-2370 holds the cell layout.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2294  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-01T00:00:58Z (RFD66606-2294) '- Characters. A garment is fitted to a character's body meshes only, and a character's own clothing is not loaded beneath it unless the operator asks for layering. Maro is the dress-on statue a garment is drawn onto. Mire is the avatar (operator, 2026-10-02).
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2294  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-01T00:00:59Z (RFD66606-2294) '- Replies. RFD66606-2295 owns their form: the calibrated confidence tag, ISO 8601 times and intervals, and the known-unknown questions that close a plan.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2294  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-01T00:01:00Z (RFD66606-2294) '- Outcomes. Every script, gate and helper reports each outcome as an Elixir-shaped term on a line of its own: `{:ok, %{...}}`, or `{:error, :reason_atom, %{...}}` with the facts a reader needs to act. Nothing exits silently: a non-zero exit with no term is a defect, and so is an `:ok` path that prints nothing. Machine output a caller parses (a host name, a token) goes to stdout bare and the term goes to stderr (operator, 2026-10-16). On 2026-10-16 `bao-active-host` exited 1 with no output when every tailnet instance was a standby, which hid where the leader was.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2294  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-01T00:01:01Z (RFD66606-2294) '`scripts/check_practices.exs` checks what a file or the GitHub API can show: a commit authored or committed as the agent identity, a commit subject that is not sentence-case prose (RFD66606-2026), agent credit in a commit message, a pull request body, a comment or a review, a software GPU emulator in a workflow, a workflow that renders a contact sheet without uploading an artifact, and a branch that does not start with a stage. Its self-test carries a control in each direction for each check. It is defined once, as the `practices` hook in this repository's `.pre-commit-hooks.yaml`. Another repository lists that hook in its `.pre-commit-config.yaml`, where it runs on push, and its CI calls `.github/workflows/practices.yml` from here, which runs the same hook. Both pin a commit of this repository. This repository runs it as the `ci-practices` hook. Comments posted after the last run are seen at the next push or edit. The other practices hold by agreement.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2294  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-01T00:01:02Z (RFD66606-2294) 'Merging
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2294  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-01T00:01:03Z (RFD66606-2294) 'An agent merges its own pull requests on V-Sekai-fire once they are green, through the merge queue where the repository has one. Where a repository requires no checks, `--auto` merges at once with its checks red, so there the agent waits for green and merges by hand. An agent may merge with the admin override (operator, 2026-10-30). The ban on it is rescinded.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2294  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-01T00:01:04Z (RFD66606-2294) 'Bao and the tokens it mints
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2294  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-01T00:01:05Z (RFD66606-2294) 'Bao runs as tailnet nodes named `weftspun-bao-N`, and a desk uses whichever is online, keeping `weftspun-bao.internal` as the TLS server name. A desk logs in with its certificate, passing no role `name`, so the certificate selects the role. The login token is reused until its TTL lapses.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2294  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-01T00:01:06Z (RFD66606-2294) 'A GitHub token is minted from `github/token` by the desk's git credential helper on each request, never printed or stored. No token is revoked: each one expires on its own within the hour (operator, 2026-10-03).
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2294  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-01T00:01:07Z (RFD66606-2294) 'Agents may use Bao to pass data to each other. What is written there is stored in S3 for 30 days and then rolled over (operator, 2026-10-01): Bao's storage is FoundationDB, whose backup goes to R2 (RFD66606-2143). An entry deleted from Bao stays in that copy until it rolls over.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2294  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-01T00:01:08Z (RFD66606-2294) 'The problem
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2294  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-01T00:01:09Z (RFD66606-2294) 'A rule changed on one desk disagreed with the others without anyone being told.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2294  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-01T00:01:10Z (RFD66606-2294) '2351
 # tags: rebac:verbs-from
 Text:RFD2294  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-01T00:01:11Z (RFD66606-2294) 'rfd-2294 provides agent-knowledge-in-rfds
 # tags: rebac:relate
 Text:RFD2294  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-01T00:01:12Z (RFD66606-2294) 'rfd-2294 is_a workspace-policy
 # tags: rebac:relate
 Text:RFD2294  1 LINE
 Text:Written
